# Video files are deliberately NOT committed. The simulated camera source is
# an existing DeepStream sample read from its install path at run time.
# See media/README.md for the rationale.
media/*.mp4
media/*.mov
media/*.h264
media/*.mkv
media/*.avi

# TensorRT engines and their build/benchmark artifacts are deliberately NOT
# committed. An engine is a machine-specific binary: it is valid only for the
# TensorRT version, GPU architecture and optimisation profile that built it, so
# a committed engine would be unusable on any other machine and unverifiable on
# this one. Regenerate with scripts/build_engines.sh. See models/README.md.
models/engines/

# Local scratch output
*.log
*.dot

# Per-machine Claude Code settings. Currently ignored only via the user's
# global gitignore, so a clone on another machine would otherwise track it.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Editor and OS cruft
*~
*.swp
.DS_Store

# Per-frame KITTI metadata written by the Milestone 5 verification runs -- the
# detector dump and the three tracker dumps. Regenerated on every run; never
# committed.
models/detections/
models/tracks/
models/tracks_terminated/
models/tracks_shadow/

# Per-frame restricted-zone evidence, written by the verification probe rather
# than by deepstream-app. Regenerated on every run; never committed.
models/zone/

# The Triton model repository's ENTRY (config.pbtxt) is committed -- it is
# application configuration. The model artifact under it is not: model.plan is
# the machine-specific FP16 engine, bind-mounted read-only at run time.
models/triton_model_repo/*/*/model.plan

# Milestone 9 surveillance events: JSON Lines written by analytics_probe on each
# run and truncated at the start of the next one. Runtime output, not source --
# representative event lines are quoted in docs/milestone-09-events.md instead.
models/events/

# Milestone 8 edge telemetry: tegrastats logs, the 1 Hz host sampler, the
# timestamped application log and the run summaries. Small text, regenerated by
# scripts/measure_edge.sh on every run, never committed -- the figures that
# matter are quoted in docs/milestone-08-*.md instead.
models/edge/

# Compiled verification tooling. tools/analytics_probe.cpp is committed; the
# binary is a build artifact, is machine-specific, and is rebuilt on demand by
# scripts/ds_common.sh.
build/

# Python bytecode cache from the analysis scripts
__pycache__/
